From d22e3976f3bceafcaaef6de6f63e5d79e97619c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HOTTY Agent <hotty@neuroplast.io>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 14:51:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] blitz-dom, blitz-paint: form controls follow the used color
 scheme

Fields were white and buttons light grey on every page, and checkboxes and
radio buttons white with the text color as their accent, so a page with
`color-scheme: dark` showed light controls. Chromium and Firefox take
these controls' colors from the CSS system colors, which resolve in the
element's used color scheme, and Stylo already resolves them that way.

The UA stylesheet now gives fields `Field` and `FieldText`, and buttons
`ButtonFace` and `ButtonText`. Their borders are the ones Chromium draws
in each scheme, through `light-dark()`. A page's own colors still win.

Checkboxes and radio buttons are drawn whole by form_controls.rs in the
element's used color scheme (BaseDocument::used_color_scheme: the scheme
Stylo resolves system colors in), with the colors Chromium draws for
`accent-color: auto` (Stylo's Servo build has no `accent-color`), checked,
unchecked and disabled, and Chromium's geometry: a 13px box, a 1px
border, 2px corners, and a check mark and a dot in proportion to the box.
The UA stylesheet sizes them as Chromium does and paints nothing of the
box under them; they were 20px and 18px, over the field's background and
border.

In a light scheme, buttons are Stylo's ButtonFace, #DCDCDC, where they
were #EFEFEF.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
